          "email": "johgras@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-11-20 18:18:28.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-21273 tests: force round-robin in sanity test_0e",
        "message": "LU-21273 tests: force round-robin in sanity test_0e\n\nsanity test_0e creates two directories in ROOT and fails if they land\non the same MDT, which assumes the client places them round-robin. The\nclient only does that while the MDTs are within lmv.*.qos_threshold_rr\n(5% by default) of each other, otherwise it uses weighted-random QoS\nplacement and the two mkdirs can pick the same MDT. ZFS MDTs only\nestimate their free inode count, so even empty MDTs are far apart:\n5.1M vs 7.4M inodes, about 31%, on a 4-MDT ZFS rig. The test failed\nthere in 3 of 20 runs with \"directories are on the same MDT\".\n\nSet lmv.*.qos_threshold_rr=100 for the test so mkdir always uses\nround-robin, and restore the old value with stack_trap. The test then\npassed 20 of 20 runs.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs mdscount=2 mdtcount=4\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity env=ONLY=0e,ONLY_REPEAT=20\nSigned-off-by: John Grasso <johgras@amazon.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I1cea5c15ae5cf6538779e32851ba41baae1aef7b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
